      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a detailed patient case study for a middle-aged man, Jack Miller, with an acute injury:\n\nPatient Profile:\n- Age: 45 years old\n- Weight: 180 lbs\n- Chief Complaint: Severe pain in the left lower extremity (thigh) due to a traumatic fall landing on his outstretched leg.\n\nVitals:\n\n* Blood Pressure: 120/80 mmHg\n* Pulse: 90 beats per minute\n* Respiratory Rate: 16 breaths per minute\n* Oxygen Saturation: 98% on 2 liters of oxygen via nasal cannula\n* Temperature: 98.6°F (37°C)\n\nDescription of Pain:\n\"I woke up in a lot of pain,\" Jack says, wincing in discomfort. \"It feels like someone punched me in the leg. The pain is a 9 out of 10, and it's getting worse with every movement.\" Jack describes the pain as a sharp, stabbing sensation that radiates down his thigh, and he reports trouble walking and weight-bearing.\n\nDemeanor:\nJack appears anxious and uncomfortable, fidgeting under the chart. He looks pale, with visible tension in his face and neck. When asked about his pain",
